    "text": "Mr. Edward Salloway"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-afe7a5",
    "offset": 2289,
    "text": "That this committee sit Tuesdays and Fridays, by three of the clock in the afternoon, in the banqueting-house, court of requests, or painted chamber, the doors being open, and the room well fitted for all comers; and that Mr. Harrington having proposed by appointment of the parliament, such others may propose as shall have the leave of the parliament."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-2c5f6b",
    "offset": 2644,
    "text": "This by friends of the commonwealth is proposed with Mr. HARRINGTON’s consent."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-51061f",
    "offset": 2724,
    "text": "The Reasons for this Proposition are these:"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-b2771c",
    "offset": 2769,
    "text": "IT is the fairest way of proposing a government, that it be first proposed to conviction, before it be imposed by power."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c62c60",
    "offset": 2891,
    "text": "THE persons herein nominated being convinced, it must necessarily have an healing effect."
  }
]